                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "MU1qu",
                      "name": "H",
                      "fill": "$plan-actual",
                      "content": "TRIGGER & TRANSITION",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.3
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "DDMxb",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$ink-60",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "position: fixed from the first paint — the header never re-mounts, it only restyles.\n\nThe stuck styles switch on when scrollY > 120px, not when the hero ends. Waiting for the hero to clear leaves the header floating with no background over the top of section 01.\n\n180ms ease-out on background-color, height and padding. Nothing else animates.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "pkwwv",
                  "name": "WHAT CHANGES, WHAT DOESN'T",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 14,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "ZoLTs",
                      "name": "H",
                      "fill": "$plan-actual",
                      "content": "WHAT CHANGES, WHAT DOESN'T",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.3
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "VYFa6",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$ink-60",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Changes: height 82 → 64, background transparent → Ink 92% + 18px backdrop blur, hairline underneath appears.\n\nDoes NOT change: content colour. Links, language and CTA stay cream in both states. The nav is cream over the dark hero and cream over the dark stuck bar, so nothing flips mid-scroll.\n\nSwaps: the status line becomes the mark + wordmark lockup.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "I5ECNO",
                  "name": "WHY THE LOCKUP APPEARS",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 14,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Cm0t8",
                      "name": "H",
                      "fill": "$plan-actual",
                      "content": "WHY THE LOCKUP APPEARS",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.3
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "DFMat",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$ink-60",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "At rest the brand is the 196px LINKNMS in the hero — the header does not need to repeat it.\n\nOnce stuck, that wordmark has scrolled away and the page has no brand on screen at all. The lockup is not decoration: it is the only linknms in the viewport for the remaining 5,000px of page.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "q1uw6W",
                  "name": "CONFLICT TO RESOLVE",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 14,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "UdkJL",
                      "name": "H",
                      "fill": "$plan-actual",
                      "content": "CONFLICT TO RESOLVE",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.3
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "I7bGIX",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$ink-60",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A fixed header and a GSAP-pinned section fight each other. The pinned scroll sequence fills the viewport, so the header will sit on top of it.\n\nEither give ScrollTrigger pinnedContainer padding equal to the header height, or hide the header for the duration of the pin. Decide before building — retrofitting this is painful.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "y5G7jI",
                  "name": "LANGUAGE",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 14,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "kJ4UR",
                      "name": "H",
                      "fill": "$plan-actual",
                      "content": "LANGUAGE",
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.3
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "F98Ft",
                      "name": "T",
                      "fill": "$ink-60",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Nine locales, so the control is a menu and not a toggle. Trigger is globe + the active code; the panel is right-aligned to the trigger.\n\nFirst visit: pick from Accept-Language, fall back to PT. Never geo-IP — a Ukrainian bricklayer on a Portuguese site should get Ukrainian, not Portuguese.\n\nPersist in a cookie, not just localStorage, so the server renders the right language on the next request and there is no flash of the wrong copy.\n\nEach locale needs a real URL (/pt/, /en/) with hreflang. A client-side-only switcher is invisible to search.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.65,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
